--rounds 2 --unwind 3
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^Round bound (static): count=4 path=4 
--
^warning: ignoring
--
fib_unsafe with N = 2. Backward-edge targets: main's final block (it reads
what both workers write) and both blocks of t1 (t2 reads i and writes j) --
count = 1 + 3. The heaviest path is t2.1 -> t1.1 -> t2.2 -> t1.2 -> main,
three backward edges, and it is a real execution: with the round-robin order
main, t1, t2 it runs t2.1 in round 1, t1.1 and t2.2 in round 2, t1.2 in round
3, and main's read can only follow in round 4. So path = 4 = N + 2 rounds to
explore everything, one more than the N + 1 at which fib_unsafe-N's bug shows
up (the calibration table): reaching one bug and covering every execution are
different depths.
